From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: initialize a window's keyboard cues at its first activation

Purpose: access-key underlines and focus rectangles stay hidden until Alt
is pressed in windows that are not dialogs (Security Center, Control Panel
items), as on XP.
XP behavior: with keyboard cues off (XP's default), a top-level window that
is activated hides its access keys; dialogs initialize them themselves.
Wine before (with 0045): windows other than dialogs kept every cue shown.
Change: with the external shell, a window activated without a UI state of
its own gets WM_CHANGEUISTATE(UIS_INITIALIZE, hide accelerators and focus),
which 0045 turns into hidden cues when keyboard cues are off.
Scope: WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/input.c b/dlls/win32u/input.c
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -2058,6 +2058,9 @@
 /*******************************************************************
  *		set_active_window
  */
+/* The keyboard-cue UI state of a window (defwnd.c). */
+static const WCHAR ui_state_prop[] = {'_','_','w','i','n','e','_','u','i','_','s','t','a','t','e',0};
+
 BOOL set_active_window( HWND hwnd, HWND *prev, BOOL mouse, BOOL focus, DWORD new_active_thread_id )
 {
     HWND previous = get_active_window();
@@ -2144,6 +2147,11 @@
         send_message( hwnd, WM_ACTIVATE,
                       MAKEWPARAM( mouse ? WA_CLICKACTIVE : WA_ACTIVE, is_iconic(hwnd) ? 0x20 : 0 ),
                       (LPARAM)previous );
+        /* Like XP, a window's first activation initializes its keyboard
+         * cues: hidden access-key underlines and focus rectangles until Alt
+         * or Tab, when keyboard cues are off (dialogs do it themselves). */
+        if (win4wine_external_shell() && !NtUserGetProp( hwnd, ui_state_prop ))
+            send_message( hwnd, WM_CHANGEUISTATE, MAKEWPARAM( UIS_INITIALIZE, UISF_HIDEACCEL | UISF_HIDEFOCUS ), 0 );
         if (NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_PARENT ) == get_desktop_window())
             NtUserPostMessage( get_desktop_window(), WM_PARENTNOTIFY, WM_NCACTIVATE, (LPARAM)hwnd );
     }
